{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "12a68172-931b-85d8-9d34-b9cf712008d0",
  "created_at": "2026-01-30T13:18:49-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Finance",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Jorge Silva",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Luis Barros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:17:03-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Finance department, Luis speaking. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:17:07-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, um, yes. I'm calling about property tax. I need a copy of a paid bill from a past year, for a refinance."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:17:15-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, we can do that. Which property, and which year?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:17:19-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, it's 180 Dixon Street, up in the North End. Um, I need the bill from two thousand twenty-four. The, the one that shows it was paid."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:17:28-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, 180 Dixon. And the name on the account?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:17:32-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Silva. Jorge Silva. S-I-L-V-A. [line breaks up] sorry, can you hear me? I'm in the car, the signal is, um, not great."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:17:39-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You cut out a little there, but I got Silva, J-O-R-G-E. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:17:44-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, yes, that's right. Sorry, mi esposa is, um, talking in the back, and the kids, they... well, we speak three languages at home, so I switch in the middle. Está bem, I mean, it's fine, I'm good."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:17:56-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, I've heard worse in this office. Let me pull up the account. [pause] Okay, I see 2024, and it shows paid in full. I can send you a copy of that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:18:06-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. Can you, um, email it? And also a confirmation that you sent it? The lender wants, well, they want something in writing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:18:13-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can email the bill, and the email itself will be your confirmation. What address should I use?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:18:19-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[crosstalk] Um, can I give it to you, sorry, you're breaking up. Can you say that again?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:18:25-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I said, what email address do you want it sent to?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:18:29-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, okay. Yeah, it's the one on the account already, I think. Can you just use that?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:18:35-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yep, there's one on file. I'll send it there today, so keep an eye out this afternoon. Check your spam folder if it doesn't show."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:18:43-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, perfect. Thank you. That's all I needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-30T13:18:46-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You got it. Good luck with the refinance."
    }
  ],
